# ACT 2 · Classroom · Scene: Blaire invites her friends to the haunted house "later that week".
# She's having fun here. The betrayal (Acts 4-5) is only seeded: Friend 1/Friend 2 glance, "don't back out", Friend 3 hesitates.
Friend1: No, no, watch this part. Watch his face. He doesn't see the cake coming.
Friend2: [pause=0.3]Oh my god. That's so mean. Play it again.
Friend3: You're going to get detention for having your phone out.
Blaire: Good morning!
Friend2: Blaire! Hiii.
Friend1: Morning. Hey, did you do the math sheet?
Blaire: Yeah! Want to see it?
Friend1: Want to "copy" it. Big difference.
Blaire: Here. Just change a few answers so it's not obvious.
Friend1: See, this is why you're my favourite.
Blaire: [pause=0.3]So. Um. Are you guys free on Friday night?
Friend1: Depends. If it's another study group, I'm sick. Very sick. Contagious.
Blaire: It's not! It's... okay. There's this old house. Nobody's lived in it for years.
Blaire: People say the lights on the second floor turn on by themselves. Every night, around midnight.
Friend3: People where?
Blaire: Just a group I'm in. Online. They know all the creepy places around here.
Friend1: A haunted house? Oh, I'm filming the entire thing.
Friend2: [pause=0.4]That sounds so fun, Blaire. We're in. Right?
Friend1: Totally in.
Friend3: [pause=0.4]...Right. Sure.
Friend1: Ghosts aren't real, by the way. Just so you know. I'll prove it.
Ghost: I'm standing right behind you.
Friend2: Send us the address. We'll bring snacks.
Friend2: And Blaire? Don't back out on us.
Blaire: I won't! I won't. I promise.
Ghost: They said yes so fast.
